<title>USA: Hybridon hits milestone in Roche alliance.</title>
<headline>Hybridon hits milestone in Roche alliance.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hybridon Inc said on Thursday that a lead compound for the treatment of human papillomavirus (HPV) in its collaboration with Hoffmann-La Roche has been selected, which triggered a milestone payment to Hybridon.</p>
<p>Hybridon said that the HPV compound, which is being designed to be applied topically, will advance to further preclinical studies later this year, with the intent of initiating human clinical trials under Roche sponsorship in 1998.</p>
<p>HPV causes genital warts, one of the most prevalent sexually transmitted diseases.</p>
<p>Hoffman-La Roche is an affiliate of Roche Holding AG.</p>
</text>
